# ASC: light enough to load, just enough to run

Apply when this workspace is ASC, the tree has `asc/bootstrap.sh`, or the task touches such a tree. Otherwise skip.

## Root `README.md` (human)

The human writes the canonical README. Agents do not create, fill, or “complete” it unless **explicitly asked**.

Each accepted README edit must make the file **lighter or clearer**, not larger. One example per idea. No plan dumps, no hypothetical files, no exhaustive matrices.

```text
❌ Unsolicited README.md patches
❌ Paste a 20-row loader table “so every case is covered”
✅ Changelog / docs / plans for the long form
✅ If asked: 3–5 rows, then stop; human continues
```

## Any ASC tree (core, ext, contrib, instance)

Ship the smallest thing that still works. Prefer fewer files, fewer always-sourced lines, fewer wrappers.

```text
❌ New include “for completeness” with no caller
❌ Eager *.inc.sh for a function one action/hook needs
❌ Document or create a file that does not exist yet
✅ Match an existing script; stop when the action runs
✅ Lazy or in-entry-point only after a real caller exists
```

Ask before adding a loader, hook, wrapper, or global. Changelog may be long; README and runtime paths may not.
